# Shell scripts run inside Linux containers — CRLF would make them unrunnable
# ("bad interpreter"), so pin them to LF regardless of the checkout platform.
*.sh text eol=lf

# The coordinator protocol and the guard arrived here on 2026-08-29 from a repo
# that pinned core.autocrlf=false so they restored byte-identical. This box's
# global setting is autocrlf=true, which would rewrite every one of these LF
# files to CRLF on the next checkout. Pin them instead of relying on a repo-local
# git config that a fresh clone would not inherit.
.claude/** text eol=lf
